COMP3005 Database Management Systems: A3

Teodor Ristic 101336978

This is a java program that connects to postgres w/ JDBC and performs CRUD operations
on the given "students" table.

Demo Video: https://youtu.be/7RQEBWlWuD4

FILES:
- "database/createDatabase.sql" creates the database
- "database/schema.sql" creates the "students" table mentioned above
- "database/seed.sql" inserts the starting data
- "app/StudentOperations.java" the application
- "lib/postgresql-42.7.14.jar" the PostgreSQL JDBC driver

SETUP:
1. In pgAdmin, run "createDatabase.sql" on the postgres database.
2. Open a Query Tool on "students_db" and run schema.sql, then seed.sql.
3. In StudentOperations.java program, change "password" to your PostgreSQL password.

COMPILING PROG.:

Terminal:
1. javac -d out app/StudentOperations.java
2. java -cp "out:lib/postgresql-42.7.14.jar" StudentOperations

Windows OS: out;lib/postgresql-42.7.14.jar (for second command)

IDE:
1. Open the project in an IDE
2. Add the jar in lib as an external library
3. Run StudentOperations.java.

FUNCTIONS (StudentOperations):
- "getAllStudents()" prints every student in the table
- "addStudent(first_name, last_name, email, enrollment_date)" inserts a new student
- "updateStudentEmail(student_id, new_email)" updates the email of the student with that id
- "deleteStudent(student_id)" deletes the student with that id